                <pb facs="0428" n="114" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg114"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/1009</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Roumania</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Vopicka</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Bucharest</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-09-29T15:00:00+01:44">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">September 29, 1914, 3 p.m.</hi>
                    </date>
                    <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 5:40 p.m.</hi>] </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>Referring to my cable of September 14, noon.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d212-f1"/> It
                    appears probable that, as a result of Crown Council which is to be held next
                    Wednesday, war will be declared by Roumania against Germany and Austria-Hungary.
                    Great popular demonstrations are held here daily in favor of such action.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Vopicka</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
